WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.607
For years drug action was pictured as occupancy. Induced proximity

00:00:05.607 --> 00:00:10.664
instead asks whether a molecule can bring two biological partners together.

00:00:14.883 --> 00:00:20.010
A bifunctional agent can link a target protein to an

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:25.136
E3 ligase and initiate ubiquitination, redirecting the cell's own disposal machinery.

00:00:29.425 --> 00:00:34.731
The two proteins must form a productive complex. Linker length, orientation

00:00:34.731 --> 00:00:40.036
and cooperativity matter in ways simple binary affinity does not describe.

00:00:44.425 --> 00:00:48.928
A bridge that dissociates too fast fails to act, while one

00:00:48.928 --> 00:00:53.431
that never releases may fail to turn over. Residence time becomes functional.

00:00:57.258 --> 00:01:01.868
Induced proximity can also relocalise or stabilize a protein, revealing

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:06.477
that the real modality is the event the molecule causes.

00:01:10.383 --> 00:01:15.393
The column follows the move from simply blocking function to engineering

00:01:15.393 --> 00:01:20.403
a testable cellular event with selectivity, exposure and resistance in view.
